Looking at this problem, I need to determine whether a rational function $f \in \mathbb{R}(x_1, \ldots, x_n)$ that is continuous on all of $\mathbb{R}^n$ must be Lipschitz on the unit ball.

**Answer leak check:** The problem text contains only the problem statement and procedural constraints. No solutions, sketches, or answer values are present.

